{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.abs_fig8Term_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.abs_fig8Term_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.lean#L135-L139","doc":"**Bar invariance of the modulus**, the form the probe measures (ratio `1.0`\nto `5.9e-49` at the substrate pair). Immediate from the exact invariance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.abs_fig8Factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.abs_fig8Factor","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.lean#L126-L133","doc":"The modulus of a factor, over `ℝ` with `0 < q`: `|(1 − qʲ)(1 − q⁻ʲ)| =\n(qʲ − 1)²/qʲ`, manifestly bar-symmetric via `fig8Factor_bar_invariant`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.fig8Factor_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.fig8Factor_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.lean#L117-L124","doc":"Over `ℝ` with `0 < q`, every factor is `≤ 0`. Archimedean: needs the\nordering, so it takes `ℝ` and sits on that side of the wall. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.fig8Factor_eq_neg_sq_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.fig8Factor_eq_neg_sq_div","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.lean#L105-L115","doc":"`(1 − qʲ)(1 − q⁻ʲ) = −(qʲ − 1)² / qʲ`.\n\nStated with a division rather than a square root so it remains over a generic\nfield; the `ℝ`-specific sign consequence is separated out below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.fig8Term_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.fig8Term_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.lean#L91-L101","doc":"**The whole term is fixed by the bar involution**, exactly — not merely in\nmodulus. `T_n(q⁻¹) = T_n(q)` for every `n`.\n\nThis is the front-(a) result: for `J(4₁)` the two members of a bar-pair are\ninterchangeable, so moving the evaluation from `q₀` to `q₀⁻¹` changes nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.fig8Factor_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.fig8Factor_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.lean#L80-L89","doc":"**Each factor is fixed by the bar involution.** The involution `q ↦ q⁻¹`\nswaps the two brackets of `(1 − qʲ)(1 − q⁻ʲ)`, and multiplication commutes.\n\nGeneric per §7c — any field, and **no** `q ≠ 0` hypothesis is needed: Lean's\n`0⁻¹ = 0` makes it hold at `q = 0` too. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.fig8Term_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.fig8Term_succ","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.lean#L75-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.fig8Term_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.fig8Term_zero","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.fig8Term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.fig8Term","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.lean#L67-L71","doc":"The figure-eight cyclotomic term `T_n(q) = ∏_{j=1}^{n} (1 − qʲ)(1 − q⁻ʲ)`,\nthe `n`-th summand of `J(4₁; q) = Σ_n (q;q)_n (q⁻¹;q⁻¹)_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.fig8Factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.fig8Factor","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Fig8CyclotomicBarInvariance.lean#L63-L65","doc":"One factor of the figure-eight cyclotomic term: `(1 − qʲ)(1 − q⁻ʲ)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}